1
00:00:04,171 --> 00:00:05,631
<i>My name's Pavi.</i>

2
00:00:05,756 --> 00:00:07,549
<i>And this here is Geet.</i>

3
00:00:08,217 --> 00:00:11,219
<i>Trust me,
the last thing we want is</i>

4
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:13,388
<i>to be noticed by anyone
in the Brigade.</i>

5
00:00:13,805 --> 00:00:18,434
So the Avatar's cruel reign
over humanity finally ended.

6
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:22,104
Our ancestors banded together
and created...

7
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:25,067
the Seven Havens.

8
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:30,614
That's an unregistered bender!

9
00:00:39,915 --> 00:00:40,958
The Avatar...

10
00:00:42,626 --> 00:00:45,462
You can't have found the Avatar
because...

11
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:49,216
<i>I already have.</i>

12
00:00:56,807 --> 00:00:58,308
Huh?

13
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:00,351
Whoa!

14
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,665
Did you see that? I'm awesome!

15
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:27,588
Good work, Cadets.

16
00:01:27,713 --> 00:01:30,506
Take the rest of the day
and enjoy the festival.

17
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:32,300
- Off with ya!
- Wanna play hunt the Avatar?

18
00:01:32,301 --> 00:01:33,427
Bet I'm faster than you!

19
00:01:33,552 --> 00:01:35,386
- Only if I'm not it!
- Okay, then you're on!

20
00:01:35,387 --> 00:01:37,014
Winner gets the first Kulfi Pop!

21
00:01:38,515 --> 00:01:40,474
Nisha,
that was reckless.

22
00:01:40,475 --> 00:01:41,851
You absolutely

23
00:01:41,852 --> 00:01:43,603
- cannot bend in public.
- Cannot bend in public.

24
00:01:43,604 --> 00:01:45,814
But these kids are amateurs
compared to me.

25
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:47,940
That is not the point.

26
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:49,567
Never mind.

27
00:01:49,568 --> 00:01:51,277
I need to get
to the festival ground.

28
00:01:51,278 --> 00:01:54,030
Apparently, there's a ruckus
with some crazed beetles.

29
00:01:54,031 --> 00:01:57,283
Captain Karthik,
can I please go to the festival?

30
00:01:57,284 --> 00:01:58,951
Nisha, you know the answer.

31
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:00,871
I promise I won't bend
a single pebble!

32
00:02:00,996 --> 00:02:03,874
I can't do my job
if I have to keep one eye on you

33
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:05,082
the entire time.

34
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:06,751
What's the point
of being the Avatar

35
00:02:06,752 --> 00:02:08,919
if I'm hiding in my room
all the time?!

36
00:02:09,713 --> 00:02:12,549
Your day in the sun will come,
young one.

37
00:02:13,425 --> 00:02:15,509
Just... not today.

38
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:30,400
No one understands us, Ruhi.

39
00:02:32,611 --> 00:02:34,362
"Just not today."

40
00:02:34,363 --> 00:02:35,697
Or any day!

41
00:02:38,075 --> 00:02:40,243
How can I be a hero
to the people...

42
00:02:41,495 --> 00:02:44,289
if I can't be around

43
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:46,457
any people?!

44
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:54,424
Ha!

45
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:33,505
Why?

46
00:03:34,047 --> 00:03:36,425
Why do you look like... me?

47
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:39,176
Uh, if anyone
looks like someone,

48
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:40,636
you look like me.

49
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:42,346
So we must be...

50
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:43,556
- Twins?
- Twins.

51
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:50,062
W-wait, hold on.
You were bending...

52
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:51,273
O-oh, no, you-you didn't see--

53
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:53,357
You were bending
all the elements!

54
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:55,276
Me? Bend all four elements?

55
00:03:55,277 --> 00:03:57,069
The heat must be getting to you!

56
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:58,779
I don't understand.

57
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,907
I thought I was the only one.

58
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:02,534
"The only one"?

59
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:05,245
- You mean, you can--
- Wait, I didn't say--

60
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,371
Yes, you did.

61
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:07,748
Are you really like me?

62
00:04:07,873 --> 00:04:09,832
No! I mean, no.

63
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:10,751
No.

64
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:14,004
Yeah, you are definitely lying.
You're not very good at it.

65
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:16,547
I don't want any attention
from the Brigade.

66
00:04:16,548 --> 00:04:19,550
Everyone is preparing
for the festival!

67
00:04:19,551 --> 00:04:20,593
It is just us.

68
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:22,721
I promise I won't tell anyone.

69
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:25,639
Which district are you from?

70
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,600
I live here in the Compound.

71
00:04:27,601 --> 00:04:29,436
Captain Karthik found me
three years ago

72
00:04:29,561 --> 00:04:31,021
and trains me in secret.

73
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:33,398
I don't remember anything
before that.

74
00:04:33,815 --> 00:04:36,650
I don't remember
where I'm from either.

75
00:04:36,651 --> 00:04:37,902
Really?

76
00:04:37,903 --> 00:04:39,487
So we are twins!

77
00:04:39,488 --> 00:04:41,114
You can show me what you can do,

78
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:42,449
I won't tell anyone.

79
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,911
Fine. It's just...

80
00:04:46,661 --> 00:04:48,663
I'm tired of being different.

81
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:51,917
I wanna know
if there's anyone else like me.

82
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:03,969
Now show me the other elements.

83
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:05,721
I... I have no idea

84
00:05:05,722 --> 00:05:06,681
what you're talking about.

85
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:09,016
Seriously,
you're a terrible liar.

86
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:10,684
You say that
like it's a bad thing!

87
00:05:10,685 --> 00:05:12,521
Okay, I'll go first.

88
00:05:14,773 --> 00:05:15,899
So...

89
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:18,443
are you really like me?

90
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:36,002
Pavi, catch!

91
00:05:36,878 --> 00:05:39,046
I got it, Nisha!

92
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:51,141
Did you--

93
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:52,185
Yeah.

94
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:54,646
Hi...

95
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:56,565
Nisha.

96
00:05:57,566 --> 00:05:58,733
Hi back...

97
00:05:59,818 --> 00:06:00,776
Pavi.

98
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:04,488
We loved playing catch.

99
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:08,034
Well, Pavi, instead of catch,
how about a game of tag?

100
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:09,743
Tag?

101
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:11,246
I'm sorry, what is--

102
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:12,622
Tag! You're it!

103
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:20,296
Oh, wow. Y-your leg.
How did I miss that?

104
00:06:20,297 --> 00:06:21,463
Are you okay?

105
00:06:21,464 --> 00:06:23,633
Oh, I was born this way.

106
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:26,552
Ha!

107
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:29,430
Now you're it!

108
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:42,067
So... how are we both like this?

109
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:43,777
Well, as long as I can remember,

110
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:47,198
I've been secretly training
to be the Avatar.

111
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:49,534
But if I'm the Avatar...

112
00:06:50,118 --> 00:06:51,244
what does that make you?

113
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:52,912
Nisha!

114
00:06:52,913 --> 00:06:54,955
Where are you?! I need to--

115
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:56,540
Ow!

116
00:06:57,542 --> 00:06:59,209
Karthik, look!

117
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:00,836
I have a twin!

118
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:07,968
Pavi,

119
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:10,472
Nisha told me quite a lot
about you.

120
00:07:10,597 --> 00:07:12,432
Do you see my cup of tea?

121
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:16,061
Would you mind showing me
a little of your abilities?

122
00:07:16,937 --> 00:07:19,731
I swear to you,
I mean you no harm.

123
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:23,777
It's okay.

124
00:07:43,046 --> 00:07:44,672
Two Avatars?

125
00:07:44,673 --> 00:07:48,467
A-are you going to make me join

126
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:50,095
the Bending Brigade?

127
00:07:50,762 --> 00:07:52,097
What you are

128
00:07:52,764 --> 00:07:55,849
is more important
than the entire Brigade.

129
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:57,601
Both you and Nisha.

130
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:59,269
I've had to hide like you.

131
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:01,106
The Brigade thinks
I'm Captain Karthik's

132
00:08:01,231 --> 00:08:02,148
bending-less assistant.

133
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:04,024
But soon they'll know the truth.

134
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:06,276
Only a few people know
Nisha's secret.

135
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:09,363
And I guess that now means
you do too, Jae.

136
00:08:09,364 --> 00:08:10,532
Uh-huh.

137
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:13,033
Uh, I am processing
all of this...

138
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:15,285
f-f-fantastically.

139
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:17,706
I can't be an Avatar.

140
00:08:18,081 --> 00:08:19,457
I'm no warrior.

141
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:22,084
And the last one
doomed the world,

142
00:08:22,085 --> 00:08:23,294
didn't she?

143
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:26,213
Korra wasn't a normal Avatar.

144
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:28,215
Most recorded history is lost,

145
00:08:28,216 --> 00:08:30,968
but what we have found
points to...

146
00:08:32,511 --> 00:08:35,764
Avatar Korra caused
the Cataclysm.

147
00:08:35,765 --> 00:08:38,809
Because of the destruction
Korra wrought,

148
00:08:38,934 --> 00:08:41,354
the Avatar became
an enemy of the world.

149
00:08:41,813 --> 00:08:43,647
Regardless of what Korra did,

150
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:46,650
I believe in a more hopeful
version of the Avatar

151
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:48,611
than the Seven Havens do.

152
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:51,114
For thousands of years,

153
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:54,033
the Avatar reincarnated
again and again

154
00:08:54,034 --> 00:08:55,826
to defend the people
of the world,

155
00:08:55,827 --> 00:08:58,663
no matter their class
or their station.

156
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:01,081
That's the kind of Avatar
I wanna be.

157
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:03,585
I had no idea there was more
to the legend.

158
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:05,253
Most people don't.

159
00:09:06,004 --> 00:09:08,630
Have there ever been
twin Avatars?

160
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,550
Never before you two.

161
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:13,552
But how else can we explain
your likeness to Nisha

162
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:14,803
and your abilities?

163
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:17,222
You never considered
you're an Avatar?

164
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:20,226
I guess I always feared I was...

165
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:22,187
but hoped I wasn't.

166
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:23,563
Join us.

167
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:25,105
Train with your sister

168
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:26,983
and become
a fully-fledged Avatar.

169
00:09:27,901 --> 00:09:31,112
But you don't need me,
you have an Avatar!

170
00:09:31,529 --> 00:09:33,947
She's me, but not a mess!

171
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,992
I spend my time collecting rocks

172
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:38,536
and introducing myself to bugs!

173
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:40,413
I'm a nobody.

174
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:41,873
Just a fluke.

175
00:09:42,457 --> 00:09:45,626
I learned a long time ago
not to believe in coincidences.

176
00:09:45,627 --> 00:09:46,628
Pavi, listen to me.

177
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:48,671
You are important.

178
00:09:48,797 --> 00:09:51,841
Pavi, together
we can be unstoppable.

179
00:09:51,966 --> 00:09:53,802
We can fix the world.

180
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:56,887
Okay, well, this has been fun,

181
00:09:56,888 --> 00:10:00,557
but I should really get back
to my cave.

182
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:02,352
Geet and I have
big dinner plans.

183
00:10:07,941 --> 00:10:09,526
By the Havens...

184
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:50,066
Yuy, get those water barrels
to the launching bay!

185
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,819
Chung, are you an earthbender
or are your feet made of mud?

186
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:53,861
Let's move!

187
00:10:53,862 --> 00:10:55,864
Go, your Haven needs you!

188
00:10:55,989 --> 00:10:57,281
- You heard the captain!
- Sir,

189
00:10:57,282 --> 00:10:58,700
I request to join my squad
out on the front.

190
00:10:58,825 --> 00:11:01,536
Jae, what you've learned
can never be spoken about.

191
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:04,164
All I want right now
is to help my people.

192
00:11:05,248 --> 00:11:06,040
Good.

193
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:07,457
Now get to your squad,

194
00:11:07,458 --> 00:11:08,459
Airbender!

195
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:13,047
Take Pavi to your room
where it's safe.

196
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:17,426
Wait! Captain!

197
00:11:17,427 --> 00:11:19,345
Captain, I'm ready.

198
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:21,306
Absolutely not, Nisha.

199
00:11:21,431 --> 00:11:23,808
Isn't this what you've been
training me for?

200
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:25,476
To save the Haven?

201
00:11:25,602 --> 00:11:27,269
The Brigade
has this storm covered.

202
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:28,729
Ellora's not ready for you.

203
00:11:28,730 --> 00:11:31,148
They don't know me! Or Pavi!

204
00:11:31,149 --> 00:11:32,733
If they just got a chance--

205
00:11:32,734 --> 00:11:35,319
Introducing you
in the middle of a disaster

206
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,279
will only feed the chaos.

207
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,697
End of discussion.

208
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:39,532
But, Karthik--

209
00:11:39,657 --> 00:11:40,658
"Captain."

210
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:43,036
Remember your place, Nisha.

211
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:58,342
Ugh!

212
00:12:00,345 --> 00:12:01,471
Nisha, let's head back.

213
00:12:01,596 --> 00:12:02,847
We're going.

214
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:05,058
Right, going somewhere safe.

215
00:12:05,183 --> 00:12:06,391
Probably underground.

216
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:07,518
Oh, I know a great hole.

217
00:12:07,644 --> 00:12:10,437
- No! We're going out there!
- Oh, yeah, well,

218
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:13,607
didn't your teacher-dad-boss
just say that's forbidden?

219
00:12:13,608 --> 00:12:14,859
I know, but...

220
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:16,986
I just... feel in my heart

221
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:19,781
this is what the Avatar
is supposed to do.

222
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:23,034
Don't you?

223
00:12:27,372 --> 00:12:29,207
Come with me.

224
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:31,459
Let's save Ellora together.

225
00:12:32,502 --> 00:12:35,671
Nisha, this is your life,
not mine.

226
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:37,047
What are you saying?

227
00:12:37,048 --> 00:12:39,383
You haven't seen Ellora like me.

228
00:12:39,384 --> 00:12:42,262
They think the Avatar
is a monster!

229
00:12:42,387 --> 00:12:44,639
Is that how you see me?

230
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,557
No! How could I?

231
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:49,142
But... I'm no hero.

232
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:51,979
I was just trying to help
my friend Sang,

233
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,148
and then my whole life
fell apart.

234
00:12:54,983 --> 00:12:57,317
I'm not an Avatar.

235
00:12:59,487 --> 00:13:01,656
I've been alone for so long.

236
00:13:01,781 --> 00:13:05,033
I thought I found someone
who finally understands.

237
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:07,245
Someone who could be family.

238
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:08,830
I was wrong.

239
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:11,666
Nisha, no. Please, wait!

240
00:13:20,258 --> 00:13:22,135
This isn't our world, Geet.

241
00:13:22,802 --> 00:13:24,512
And it's never gonna be.

242
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:31,226
Quick! Close the doors!

243
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:32,936
I have a baby!

244
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:34,856
- Get inside!
- Get to shelter!

245
00:13:39,694 --> 00:13:40,987
Come on! Come on!

246
00:13:41,112 --> 00:13:42,529
We gotta keep going!

247
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:45,158
Oh, no!

248
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:52,206
They need my help!

249
00:14:06,179 --> 00:14:07,220
I did it, Ruhi!

250
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:08,890
Ugh!

251
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,851
Ah!

252
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:24,529
I know, Geet.

253
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:27,200
But Nisha and the Brigade
have it covered.

254
00:14:37,752 --> 00:14:39,253
Hey! Are you okay?

255
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:41,963
Are... aren't you scared?

256
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:44,508
Oh, I am terrified.

257
00:14:44,509 --> 00:14:47,011
But I can help people,
so I'm out here.

258
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:48,471
Ulan!

259
00:14:54,394 --> 00:14:56,437
Ugh. Don't you start.

260
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:03,069
<i>Those kids
are amazing together.</i>

261
00:15:03,528 --> 00:15:05,028
<i>So brave.</i>

262
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:06,906
<i>Maybe with Nisha,</i>

263
00:15:07,782 --> 00:15:09,992
<i>this could all be
a little less scary.</i>

264
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:23,172
Brace the gates!

265
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:40,647
Nice of you to join us,
squad leader!

266
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:42,400
Is everyone okay?

267
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:55,496
Let's join Commander Bountan.

268
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:08,091
Commander!

269
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:20,980
We're doomed!

270
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:27,820
How are we gonna survive?

271
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:55,430
What nightmare is this?!

272
00:17:02,188 --> 00:17:04,565
Commander, what are your orders?

273
00:17:05,148 --> 00:17:06,858
Run!

274
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:08,444
Commander!

275
00:17:12,365 --> 00:17:14,366
Get back, you demon!

276
00:17:37,473 --> 00:17:39,141
Brigade,
regroup on me!

277
00:17:39,684 --> 00:17:43,228
Whatever this thing is,
I need defensive barriers now!

278
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:45,523
You heard our Captain, let's go!

279
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:25,020
Hi!

280
00:18:25,021 --> 00:18:26,855
I thought you were scared.

281
00:18:26,856 --> 00:18:27,982
I was!

282
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:29,483
I still am!

283
00:18:29,609 --> 00:18:30,775
But I'm here with you.

284
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,027
Ah!

285
00:18:32,028 --> 00:18:33,321
What is that thing?!

286
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:41,077
I don't know,
but it either likes us

287
00:18:41,078 --> 00:18:43,039
or really hates us.

288
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:48,919
How's your earthbending?

289
00:18:49,045 --> 00:18:50,588
It's my best element!

290
00:18:50,713 --> 00:18:52,757
Same! Let's go together!

291
00:19:23,204 --> 00:19:25,665
Uh... Pavi?

292
00:19:26,207 --> 00:19:27,833
Now I'm scared.

293
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:30,585
Me too.
But extra more scared now.

294
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:40,429
<i>- What's going on?
- Where are we?</i>

295
00:20:01,492 --> 00:20:03,785
Is it done?

296
00:20:03,786 --> 00:20:05,287
Did it pass?

297
00:20:08,374 --> 00:20:10,041
Search for survivors.

298
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:11,752
I'm gonna do a perimeter check.

299
00:20:16,048 --> 00:20:18,007
It's over, I think.

300
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:19,926
What was that scary zappy thing?

301
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:23,347
No idea. It looked like
it was made of... energy?

302
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:25,641
Ugh.

303
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:29,979
Hi.

304
00:20:34,567 --> 00:20:37,695
Captain! Uh,
we were just out for a...

305
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,904
Whatever
that nightmare was,

306
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:42,574
we have you two
to thank for its demise.

307
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:43,826
Well done, Nisha.

308
00:20:45,453 --> 00:20:48,371
You're clearly not the "mess"
you think you are, Pavi.

309
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:50,665
Captain Karthik,
we found the commander!

310
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:53,668
Go back to the Brigade Compound,
both of you.

311
00:20:55,337 --> 00:20:56,338
Come on!

312
00:20:57,506 --> 00:20:58,841
Ugh.

313
00:21:07,725 --> 00:21:10,853
Commander, it’s me. Karthik.

314
00:21:12,521 --> 00:21:14,231
It is coming.

315
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:15,483
What's coming?

316
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:20,362
Commander!
Somebody bring a stretcher!

317
00:21:21,614 --> 00:21:23,365
Did you see the old guy's eyes?

318
00:21:23,491 --> 00:21:24,741
What happened to him?

319
00:21:24,742 --> 00:21:26,494
No clue, but I bet it's tied

320
00:21:26,619 --> 00:21:28,037
to the energy monster.

321
00:21:28,162 --> 00:21:29,246
Let's get out of here,

322
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:31,707
or Karthik really
<i>will</i> get mad at us.

323
00:21:36,462 --> 00:21:38,797
Whoo! That was amazing, right?

324
00:21:38,798 --> 00:21:39,798
Yeah!

325
00:21:39,799 --> 00:21:40,966
Oh, uh...

326
00:21:41,091 --> 00:21:43,802
Does "amazing" not mean
what I think it means?

327
00:21:46,806 --> 00:21:49,349
We have to be ready
if that thing comes back.

328
00:21:49,350 --> 00:21:50,601
What do you say, Pavi?

329
00:21:50,726 --> 00:21:52,019
Are we in this together?

330
00:21:52,895 --> 00:21:53,896
For now,

331
00:21:54,271 --> 00:21:57,066
can we start with me
just being your, um...

332
00:21:57,900 --> 00:21:58,943
friend?

333
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:01,070
Better idea.

334
00:22:01,612 --> 00:22:03,322
Do you wanna be...

335
00:22:03,948 --> 00:22:05,324
my sister?

336
00:22:07,034 --> 00:22:08,452
Sisters it is.

337
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:17,460
That's right, Geet,

338
00:22:17,461 --> 00:22:19,921
you have a cat-sister now too!

339
00:22:19,922 --> 00:22:23,258
Or would it be cat-cousins?

340
00:22:24,343 --> 00:22:25,719
We have a lot to figure out

341
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:27,096
including...

342
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:29,973
Which cat-monkey is faster?

343
00:22:29,974 --> 00:22:31,725
Race you back to the Compound!

344
00:22:32,226 --> 00:22:33,894
Let's scramble, Geet!

